# Rule: Writing style

Documentation must be readable by someone who was not in the original conversation.

- Use complete, understandable sentences; explain the reasoning without unnecessary jargon.
- **State exactly what changed and why.** Ban vague claims like "improved the design",
  "cleaned things up", "optimized" — say what and why ("raised body contrast to 5.2:1 to meet
  WCAG AA", not "made it more accessible").
- Include concrete examples; use diagrams or structured flows (mermaid) where they help.
- Separate source rules from generated outputs; never blur the two.
- Prefer specifics over adjectives; numbers over "better/faster"; name files, tokens, and
  criteria by their real identifiers.
- Write so a user, designer, developer, or another agent can act on it cold.
